From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: fogtape <fogtape@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 07:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] deps,v8: guard Wasm-only postmortem metadata

Node 26.1's Map accessors include immediate_supertype_map, whose offset
constant exists only under V8_ENABLE_WEBASSEMBLY. The metadata generator
scans accessor text without evaluating preprocessor guards and emits an
unconditional reference, breaking iOS full and lite builds with native
Wasm disabled.

Carry the same guard into the generated C++ so that Wasm-enabled builds
retain the metadata and Wasm-disabled builds do not reference the offset.
Keep the whole guarded declaration together when deduplicating output.
---
 deps/v8/tools/gen-postmortem-metadata.py | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/deps/v8/tools/gen-postmortem-metadata.py b/deps/v8/tools/gen-postmortem-metadata.py
index 5bea9f3d2a..5b1bcd472c 100644
--- a/deps/v8/tools/gen-postmortem-metadata.py
+++ b/deps/v8/tools/gen-postmortem-metadata.py
@@ -947,7 +947,12 @@ def emit_constants(out, consts):
   for const in consts:
     name = ws.sub('', const['name'])
     value = ws.sub('', str(const['value']))  # Can be a number.
-    lines.append('V8_EXPORT int v8dbg_%s = %s;' % (name, value))
+    line = 'V8_EXPORT int v8dbg_%s = %s;' % (name, value)
+    # The accessor scan does not evaluate preprocessor conditions. This Map
+    # offset only exists with native Wasm, which jitless iOS builds disable.
+    if value == 'Map::kImmediateSupertypeOffset':
+      line = '#if V8_ENABLE_WEBASSEMBLY\n%s\n#endif' % line
+    lines.append(line)
 
   # Generate without duplicates and with preserved order.
   out.write('\n'.join(dict.fromkeys(lines)))
